<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Xiaozong of Song</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1127">1127</a>–<a href="/years/1194">1194</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Zhao Shen, Xiaozong, Zhao Bocong, Zhao Yuan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Xiaozong of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a>, personal name Zhao Shen, was the 11th emperor of the Song dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and the second of the Southern Song, a seventh-generation descendant of its founder, Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-song">Taizu</a>. Adopted by Emperor Gaozong in 1160, he came to the throne in 1162 when Gaozong abdicated, although the retired emperor remained the de facto ruler until his death in 1187. Xiaozong rehabilitated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yue-fei">Yue Fei</a> posthumously, made peace with the Jin dynasty in 1165, kept close control over his ministers and worked to stabilise the paper currency, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huizi">huizi</a>, whose value was steadied by 1175. He abdicated in 1189 in favour of his son, Emperor Guangzong, and died in 1194.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-xiaozong-of-song.jpg" alt="Emperor Xiaozong of Song" width="330" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:宋孝宗皇帝.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
